BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-188594@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260617T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260617T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260617T190000
SUMMARY:From Interest to Impact: Finding Your Place on a Nonprofit Board
LOCATION:The Living Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Impact Fund\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist On
 ly\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/188594\n\n5:00PM Re
 ception\, 5:30PM Presentation\, 6:15PM Panel Discussion\nStep into the fut
 ure of civic leadership through this dynamic program presented in partners
 hip with The 'Quin Impact Fund and United Way’s Board Connect initiative
 . Designed for emerging and established changemakers alike\, the evening w
 ill explore how nonprofit board service can become a powerful catalyst for
  impact\, innovation\, and community transformation.\n\nThe program begins
  with an interactive workshop led by United Way\, offering an inside look 
 at the responsibilities\, influence\, and opportunities that come with boa
 rd leadership. A forward-thinking panel discussion will follow\, featuring
  nonprofit leaders and governance experts including Jon Feinman of InnerCi
 ty Weightlifting\, Linda Whitlock\, Co-Chair of The 'Quin Impact Fund and
  Yolanda Coentro of the Institute for Nonprofit Practice\, moderated by Ma
 rty Martinez of United Way of Massachusetts Bay.\n\nThe evening concludes 
 with an opportunity to connect directly with local organizations actively 
 seeking new board talent—creating space for meaningful conversations\, n
 ew collaborations\, and the next generation of purpose-driven leadership.\
 n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimenta
 ry light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/188594
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Impact Fund
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-189485@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260617T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260617T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260617T183000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Echoes of Liberty
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 29 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/1
 89485\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion \nJoin us for an exclusive 
 preview of Echoes of Liberty\, an immersive Augmented Reality experience 
 that blends live performance\, history\, and soundscapes to illuminate the
  often-overlooked contributions of African Americans during the Revolution
 ary War era. Created and produced by visionary storyteller and educator Ne
 rissa Williams Scott\, Echoes of Liberty invites audiences into powerful
  narratives rooted in history\, identity\, and cultural impact.\n\nFeaturi
 ng acclaimed performances — including Golden Globe-nominated actor Blair
  Underwood as Crispus Attucks — this groundbreaking project harnesses em
 erging AR technology to bring the past vividly into the present\, creating
  an unforgettable multi-sensory experience that bridges generations throug
 h storytelling and innovation.\n\nFollowing the preview\, members will enj
 oy a dynamic conversation led by Nerissa Williams Scott alongside an estee
 med panel of scholars\, creatives\, and innovators\, including Dr. Joyce H
 ope Scott\, Clinical Professor of African American & Black Diaspora Studie
 s at Boston University\; Lynn DuVal-Luse\, Executive Producer and Emeritus
  Marketing Director of the Museum of African American History\; and Nicola
 s Robbe\, CEO and co-founder of Hoverlay\, the Augmented Reality platform 
 powering the immersive narratives of Echoes of Liberty.\n\nTogether\, the
  panel will explore the intersections of history\, technology\, education\
 , and representation — and discuss how immersive storytelling can deepen
  our understanding of the past while shaping the future of cultural engage
 ment.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Compl
 imentary light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/189485
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
